  <static seed="57" source="Library/PCC/BasicAlgebra/Exponents/exponentDivision145.pg">
    <statement><p>Simplify the following expression (do not factor)</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle\frac{{-10x^{17}y^{9}-12x^{12}y^{7}+2x^{14}y^{4}}}{{2x^{5}y^{2}}}=</m><fillin characters="32" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-5x^{12}y^{7}-6x^{7}y^{5}+x^{9}y^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>We divide each term by <m>{2x^{5}y^{2}}</m> as follows</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}
    \displaystyle\frac{{-10x^{17}y^{9}-12x^{12}y^{7}+2x^{14}y^{4}}}{{2x^{5}y^{2}}}  
    \amp  = \frac{-10x^{17}y^{9}}{2x^5y^2}+\frac{-12x^{12}y^{7}}{2x^5y^2}+\frac{2x^{14}y^{4}}{2x^5y^2}\\
     \amp  = {\left(-{\frac{10}{2}}\right)x^{12}y^{7}+\left(-{\frac{12}{2}}\right)x^{7}y^{5}+\left({\frac{2}{2}}\right)x^{9}y^{2}}\\
     \amp  = {-5x^{12}y^{7}-6x^{7}y^{5}+x^{9}y^{2}}\\
    \end{aligned}</m></p>
</solution>
